  "summary": "Nanopore-based methylation motif detection and genome-scale Z-DNA prediction offer new routes to prioritizing non-canonical sequence elements.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is computational detection of sequence-level DNA features. Snappy uses basecaller modification data from Oxford Nanopore reads in a graph-based motif enrichment approach to identify bacterial DNA methylation motifs. Z-DNA Hunter is a web server for fast, genome-scale prediction of Z-DNA forming sequences using adjustable pattern-based detection, applied to Drosophila. A preprint analyzing 3,222 human essential proteins relates CpG-island-induced regions to amino acid composition, Shannon entropy clustering, and 5' positional bias, a protein-level analysis that is less directly comparable to the two DNA-level tools. What is new is the use of nanopore basecaller modification output as input for motif discovery, paired with configurable pattern-based prediction of Z-DNA. These claims rest on published abstracts and one preprint summary, so generalization beyond these studies is not supported.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2025-11-27"
}
